\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  Lord, in the fulness of my might,\cf0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 I would for thee be strong
\par while runneth o'er each dear delight,
\par To Thee should soar my song.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  I would not give the world my heart,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 And then profess Thy love;
\par I would not feel my strength depart,
\par And then thy service prove.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. I would not with swift-winged zeal
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 on the world's errands go,
\par And labour up the heavenly hill
\par With weary feet and slow.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-360\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par    4.  O not for Thee my weak desires,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 My poorer, baser part!
\par O not for Thee my fading fires,
\par The ashes of my heart!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  O choose me in my golden time:
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 In my dear joys have part!
\par For Thee the glory of my prime,
\par The fulness of my heart.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  I cannot, Lord, too early take
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 The covenant divine;
\par O ne'er the happy heart may break
\par Whose earliest love was Thine!
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

